          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong Poincaré Lemma
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+geometry"} complex analytic geometry
            asserts that “every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            which is closed,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi dR
                    %mi ω
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{dR}\omega = 0
            %em locally
            exact,
            = succeed ".\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi U
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi dR
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega|_U = d_{dR}\kappa
          %p
            In more detail: if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+topological+space"} contractible
            then for every closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi cl
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \Omega^k_{cl}(X)
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \geq 1
            there exists a differential form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \in \Omega^{k-1}(X)
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi dR
                  %mi λ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega
                  \\,=\,
                  d_{dR} \lambda
                  \\,.
          %p
            Moreover, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            a smooth family of closed forms, there is a smooth family of
            = succeed "s" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
          %p
            This statement has several more abstract incarnations. One is that it says that on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            (or a complex
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polydisc"} polydisc
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+de+Rham+complex"} holomorphic de Rham cohomology
          %p
            Still more abstractly this says that the canonical morphisms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves+of+chain+complexes"} sheaves of chain complexes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi dR
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R} \to \Omega^\bullet_{dR}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi hol
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{C} \to \Omega^\bullet_{hol}
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+sheaf"} locally constant sheaf
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+de+Rham+complex"}> holomorphic de Rham complex
            ) is a
            = succeed "-wise" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            – hence an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
            and hence induce an equivalence in
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercohomology"} hyper
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            %em fails
            in general in complex
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Illusie12"} Illusie 12, 1.
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GAGA"} GAGA
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolutions"} resolutions
            of constant sheaves for the case over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein+geometries"} Klein geometries
            are
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BGG+resolutions"} BGG resolutions
          %p
            The Poincaré lemma is a special case of the more general statement that the pullbacks of differential forms along
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            are related by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homotopy"} chain homotopy
          %h2#Statement Statement
          %h3#over_contractible_domains Over contractible domains
          %p
          #HomotopyToChainHomotopy.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p Let
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0, f_1 \,\colon\, X \to Y
                  be a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
                  between
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ψ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi \colon [0,1] \times X \to Y
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+homotopy"} smooth homotopy
                  between them.
            %p
              Then there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homotopy"} chain homotopy
              between the induced operations of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+differential+forms"} pullback of differential forms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 0
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_0^*, f_1^*
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\Omega^\bullet(Y) \to \Omega^\bullet(X)
            %p
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complexes"} de Rham complexes
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              = succeed "\u201D:" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+operator"} homotopy operator
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi t
                      %msup
                        %mi Ψ
                        %mo *
                      %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mi d
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\psi
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\omega \mapsto
                    \\Big(
                    x
                    \\mapsto
                    \\textstyle{\int}_{[0,1]}
                    \\big(
                    \\iota_{\partial_t} \Psi^*\omega)(x)
                    \\big)
                    d t
                    \\Big)
                    \\,.
            %p
              In particular,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 0
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0^*
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1^*
              coincide on
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi dR
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 0
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi dR
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_{dR}^\bullet(f_0^*)
                    \\,\simeq\,
                    H_{dR}^\bullet(f_1^*)
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_{\partial t}
            denotes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+contraction"} contraction
            (cf.
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+calculus"} Cartan calculus
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+field"} vector field
            tangent to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration"} integration
            is that of functions with values in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            of differential forms.
          %p
          #ProofOfHomotopyToChainHomotopy.proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
            %p We compute as follows:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
