                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{l}
                    \\mathrm{d}_{X} \psi(\omega)
                    +
                    \\psi( \mathrm{d}_Y \omega )
                    \\\
                    \\;=\;
                    \\textstyle{\int}_{[0,1]}
                    \\mathrm{d}_{X}
                    \\iota_{\partial_t} \Psi^*(\omega)
                    d t
                    +
                    \\textstyle{\int}_{[0,1]}
                    \\iota_{\partial_t} \Psi^*(\mathrm{d}_Y \omega)
                    d t
                    \\\
                    \\;=\;
                    \\textstyle{\int}_{[0,1]}
                    \\mathrm{d}_{X}
                    \\iota_{\partial_t} \Psi^*(\omega)
                    d t
                    +
                    \\textstyle{\int}_{[0,1]}
                    \\iota_{\partial_t}
                    \\big(\mathrm{d}_X + \mathrm{d}_{[0,1]}\big)
                    \\Psi^*( \omega)
                    d t
                    \\\
                    \\;=\;
                    \\textstyle{\int}_{[0,1]}
                    \\iota_{\partial_t}
                    \\mathrm{d}_{[0,1]}
                    \\Psi^*(\omega)
                    d t
                    \\\
                    \\;=\;
                    \\textstyle{\int}_{[0,1]}
                    \\mathrm{d}_{[0,1]}
                    \\Psi^*(\omega)
                    \\\
                    \\;=\;
                    \\Psi_1^\ast(\omega)
                    \-
                    \\Psi_0^\ast(\omega)
                    \\\
                    \\;=\;
                    f_1^\ast \omega - f_0^\ast \omega
                    \\,,
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              where in the second step we used that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exterior+differential"} exterior differential
              commutes with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+differential+forms"} pullback of differential forms
              (
              %a{:href => "pullback+of+a+differential+form#CompatibilityWithDeRhamDifferential"}> this Prop.
              ), and in the last step the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stokes+theorem"} Stokes theorem
          %p
            The
            %strong Poincaré lemma
            proper is the special case of this statement for the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi const
                    %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_2 = const_y
            is a function constant on a point
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in Y
          %p
          .num_cor
            %h6 Corollary
            %p
              If a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              admits a smooth contraction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi id
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi id
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi Ψ
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
